        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(ai): trim private Responses exports",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Responses provider internals carried four unsupported exports in the dead-code baseline:\n\n- a stream event type used only within the shared provider\n- an options type used only within the tool converter\n- a forwarding tool-conversion export\n- a wrapper with no production callers\n\nTests also depended on the internal event type and dead wrapper instead of the callable contract that production code retains.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- keep the stream event and tool-conversion option types private\n- remove the unused wrapper and forwarding exports\n- derive the test event type from `processResponsesStream`\n- exercise `convertResponsesToolPayload` directly\n- remove the four matching dead-code baseline entries\n\nThe named `@openclaw/ai` package exports do not expose either implementation module, so this removes internal surface rather than a supported package API.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime or user-visible behavior changes. This shrinks an unsupported internal API and makes the dead-code baseline more accurate.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox: `tbx_01kxc6bywpdcg7dhyrxnqr67xy`\n- Hosted run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29211177754\n- Provider tests: 51/51 passed\n- `pnpm check:changed -- packages/ai/src/providers/openai-responses-shared.ts packages/ai/src/providers/openai-responses-shared.test.ts packages/ai/src/providers/openai-responses-tools.ts scripts/deadcode-exports.baseline.mjs`\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports`: baseline matched at 5,958 entries, down by four\n- `pnpm build`: passed\n- Fresh `gpt-5.6-sol` medium autoreview of commit `5451b777dc`: clean, confidence 0.95\n\nNo changelog entry: this is an internal dead-code cleanup with no user-visible behavior change.\n",
